From bac52760b0ef795eb5bbdc2a3985827211281a9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Tue, 21 Apr 2026 09:40:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/28] fix(tmux): fail loud when wrapped agent dies
 mid-startup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The ExecWrapper path (devbox/daytona/exitbox) can survive the 50ms+250ms
post-create health window and then exit seconds later — e.g. kubectl exec
connects, claude inside the pod dies on a missing --settings path. Before:

  - checkSessionAfterCreate saw pane alive, disabled remain-on-exit, returned nil
  - WaitForCommand saw pane_current_command=kubectl (not a shell), returned nil
  - kubectl died ~1s later; tmux destroyed the pane and session
  - TrackSessionPID warned "empty PID", witness.Start had already returned ok
  - Boot silently "succeeded" while no session existed; refinery then hung 180s

Four changes make this honest:

1. checkSessionAfterCreate keeps remain-on-exit on — a post-window death is
   now observable instead of auto-cleaned.
2. WaitForCommand polls pane_dead in its loop; on death it returns a rich
   error with exit status and a 40-line pane tail, not a generic timeout.
3. WaitForRuntimeReady does the same for the refinery prompt-probe path.
4. New WaitForAgentReady accepts ONLY the GT_AGENT_READY sentinel (plus the
   pane-dead fast-fail). When the rig has ExecWrapper configured, witness,
   refinery, and polecat Start paths use it — pane_current_command reports
   the wrapper binary, not the agent, so command-name probing false-positives.

ResolveExecWrapper is exported so the three Start paths can branch on it
without re-reading rig settings by hand.

Verified against the devbox wrapper on anvil: before, `gt rig boot devbox`
silently succeeded then timed out on refinery; after, the witness error now
surfaces the real failure ("pods polecat-pool-294ds not found") inline.

(cherry picked from commit 2a7e39fd2188f3b4a8c23e414dba015b82e17f37)
